"paragraphs": [
  "Unlike a Moving Averages (MA\u2019s) that looks backward across a certain period, renders a lagged the indicator. Atlas Adaptive Prediction Filter (AAPF) on the other hand runs a continuous Prediction Update Cycle (a mathematical linear regression State Space model derivative) that projects the price of an asset forward in time along a mean reversion predicted path. Although, the actual mathematical expression is out-of-the-scope of this discourse, but the AAPF band indicator, out of the micro-noise, while ignoring historical lag, it functions as a highly accurate, structural dynamic trendline and a lot more precise \u2018trend band\u2019.",

    "Unlike a Moving Averages (MA\u2019s) that looks backward across a certain period, renders a lagged the indicator. Atlas Adaptive Prediction Filter (AAPF) on the other hand runs a continuous Prediction Update Cycle (a mathematical linear regression State Space model derivative) that projects the price of an asset forward in time along a mean reversion predicted path. Although, the actual mathematical expression is out-of-the-scope of this discourse, but the AAPF band indicator, out of the micro-noise, while ignoring historical lag, it functions as a highly accurate, structural dynamic trendline and a lot more precise \u2018trend band\u2019.",
    "Table Data: [[\"The AAPF indicator as a band consists of two plots: AAPF-Fast & AAPF-Slow, see the figure on the right where it shows a rising green AAPF band. The upper edge of the band is the AAPF-Fast plot, whereas the lower edge is the AAPF-Slow plot; a declining red band would have the fast plot below the slow plot. Apparently, the band follows the price in somewhat similar manner as a moving average (MA), however, the AAPF band, however, follows the price much more aggressively than MA\\u2019s and become price predictive in a no-lag fashion, and therefore, highly used by institutional grade algorithms. There are few aspects of the indicator to be looked at distinctively:\\nthe color of the band tells trend (GREEN is Bull; RED is Bear),\\nthe thickness of the band that gauges the trend strength at given time,\\nthe S/R (support / resistance) structure; when the price retraces back to a degree the AAP band serves as S/R.\\n\\nNOTE The chart on the right side is an entry chart not the master.\"]]"
  ]
