"paragraphs": [
  "The slope m determines the bias of the trader\u2019s market. Even if sometime if a market is trending higher (or lower) by price, if the supporting trader\u2019s volume is absent the VWAP would reflect that. Therefore, the VWAP reflects the smart money, not just the apparent trend as its based by Volume. Usually, the morning markets or at the closing time the trends are mapped along with the trends of the smart money as the volumes are usually the highest at the market open and close.",

    "List Item: Neutral-Bias: If the slope of the VWAP near 0 (or -0.1 to +0.1) that\u2019s evidence the market is non-trending. Even if it is trending that trend is not supported by the smart money. That could be exhaustion sign. If the market is already near mean (VWAP) and the slope is near 0 and color is Goldenrod that a sign the market is in compression at a neutral point and is going to look for further data to move in some direction or breakout from this compression.",
    "List Item: Market Volumes \u2013 Open & Close: As highlighted earlier, the large institutions have very high volumes to be traded. In order or avoid market chaos they usually slice their trades in chunks, mostly they try to execute majority of their trades within the initial balance period \u2013 first 15-min to half-hour within market open (9:30a \u2013 10:00a \u2013 ET) or during the last half before market close (3:30p \u2013 4:00p \u2013 ET). Therefore, this during this time the VWAP is going to have a trending slope whereas around midday the volumes are lower and VWAP could tend to be flat."
  ]
},

