      "subsections": {},
      "paragraphs": [

    "Table Data: [[\"Salient Features\\nWhile predicting an anticipated move, the Atlas Oscillation Indicator is the first to manifest signs of a move (a bull or a bear move):\\nOscillation \\u2013 the precursor: This is one of the earliest signs of a price move (other than Atlas Bull & Bears indicator which also leads the price).\\nOscillation Plot: The curve is a solid green or a red line that oscillates within range: [0 \\u2013 100]\\nOscillation Regimes: Check the price label on the right of this top sub-panel\\nBull-Regime: Rising Green Oscillation Plot above 70 becomes bullish.\\nBear-Regime: Declining Red Oscillation Plot below 30 become bearish\\nOscillation Saturation: It is possible for the Oscillation curve to keep saturated at 0 (for bear); 100 (for bull) as the trend gets extended deeper & deeper\\nWhen the oscillators is running in saturation that does not necessarily mean that the move is over, all it shows that the market is into a deep trend. A trend could stay in saturation for many candles sometime. Reaching saturation does NOT necessarily mean a reversal.\"]]",
    "Table Data: [[\"Figure Depiction (Right Figure \\u2013 Figure: Altas Oscillation \\u2013 Rising & Falling)\\nIn the right Atlas Oscillator figure we\\u2019ve added dotted thin-line arrows to depict the Atlas Oscillation curve.\\nIn the top sub-panel (at top left and top right) there are green rising arrows trying to highlight the Atlas Oscillation solid line rising green curve.\\nIn the top middle there\\u2019s red curved arrow that shows depicting along the red solid line\\nthis red solid line is called Atlas Oscillator that is declining from a high value of about 80 declining down to 0\\nthen it stays saturated at 0 for several candles. \\nNote: that hitting 0 does NOT mean a reversal, it\\u2019s just a saturation state. \\nThe market could stay in saturation state for a long time also.\\nSame would be the case for a bull run, if the Atlas Oscillator has saturated into a value of 100, the bull run may (or may not) run for a long time.\"]]"
  ]
},

