"paragraphs": [
  "At its core, the\u00a0Atlas Bulls & Bears Indicator\u00a0is designed to show you where the real heavy hitters\u2014the institutions, central banks, and market makers\u2014are moving their capital. Retail traders simply don't have the financial muscle to move markets long-term; significant, sustained price trends only happen when large institutions inject massive liquidity pressure into the order book. This indicator captures that massive footprint in real-time, tracking how fast these large-scale market orders are aggressively sweeping through available supply and demand. By showing you exactly when institutional money flow is overwhelming the market, it fits perfectly into your overall strategy as a master trend. It takes the guesswork out of your trading by telling you precisely when to ride the coattails of institutional momentum rallies, when to stay flat during quiet neutral ranges, and when a trend has become so overextended that it's smart to take profits before a major reversal hits.",

    "The indicator Altas Bulls & Bears is plotted in the bottom sub-panel of both Master Chart as well as Entry chart. The difference would be that master chart plots represent the major rallies and moves of the day whereas the entry char plots show the microtrends and entry / exit opportunities.",
