  "h2": "",
  "h3": ""
},
{
  "type": "paragraph",
  "text": "Adaptive Feature: the band-fill (solid vs. blank) adapts to treat the validity of the S/R at any given point of time. While the band-fill is solid the S/R structure remains intact. When the band-fill is blank the S/R structure becomes invalid or rather the price is prone to passthrough the band.",
  "h1": "Atlas Adaptive Prediction Filter",
  "h2": "Atlas Propriety Features \u2013 AAPF",
  "h3": ""
},
{
  "type": "paragraph",

},
{
  "type": "paragraph",
  "text": "Predictive Feature: the band-thickness represents the strength of the trend, the position of the band relative to the price represents predictability of the price within its thickness & adaptability.",
  "h1": "Atlas Adaptive Prediction Filter",
  "h2": "Atlas Propriety Features \u2013 AAPF",
  "h3": ""
},
{
  "type": "paragraph",
  "text": "Figure : Atlas Adaptive Predictive Filter (AAPF)",
  "h1": "Atlas Adaptive Prediction Filter",
  "h2": "Atlas Propriety Features \u2013 AAPF",
  "h3": ""
},
{
  "type": "paragraph",

},
{
  "type": "paragraph",
  "text": "In an uptrend, this line acts as a dynamic support floor visa-viz in down trend acts like a dynamic resistant ceiling. Unlike a standard moving average (MA) that lags structural shifts, the AAPF band flattens out during consolidations; unlike MA the AAPF follows much more aggressively during expansions, thus providing a precise, optimized level for invalidation. The distance between the Fast & Slow filters (the band thickness) serves as an objective, mathematical metric for trend velocity and health:",
  "h1": "Atlas Adaptive Prediction Filter",
  "h2": "Predictive Trend Band S/R \u2013 Band Thickness",
  "h3": ""
},
{
  "type": "list_item",

},
{
  "type": "list_item",
  "text": "Expanding Thickness  [Trend Expansion Regime]: Indicates strong, accelerating momentum. The trend is healthy, and shorting should be strictly avoided.",
  "h1": "Atlas Adaptive Prediction Filter",
  "h2": "Predictive Trend Band S/R \u2013 Band Thickness",
  "h3": ""
},
{
  "type": "list_item",
  "text": "Compressing Thickness  [Chop Regime]: Signals that the trend is decelerating, entering structural consolidation, or preparing for a regime shift.",
  "h1": "Atlas Adaptive Prediction Filter",
  "h2": "Predictive Trend Band S/R \u2013 Band Thickness",
  "h3": ""
},
{
  "type": "paragraph",

},
{
  "type": "paragraph",
  "text": "Therefore, while trending strong, a thick AAPF band could serve as a strong S/R structure. Whereas, while trending weak, a thin AAPF band could highlight the presence of a chop zone.",
  "h1": "Atlas Adaptive Prediction Filter",
  "h2": "Predictive Trend Band S/R \u2013 Band Thickness",
  "h3": ""
},
{
  "type": "paragraph",
  "text": "The band often adapts to certain moves by giving up its fill color from green or red to as blank while the price approaches the band. In case the band gives up the color as blank, the probable S/R strength for the VWAP line decreases, potentially resulting in a breakthrough across the band.",
  "h1": "Atlas Adaptive Prediction Filter",

},
{
  "type": "paragraph",
  "text": "Important point to be considered, as also depicted in the adjacent figure, that even during a thick trending rally the band could disappear sometime and go blank. This is the adaptive feature, which implies that the AAPF band adapting to the price movement and momentum, and is NOT going to offer a S/R structure during that specific instance. This way, as a trading methodology a trader could adapt or even predict the price movements to even passthrough the band and predict a change in trend way advance in time.",
  "h1": "Atlas Adaptive Prediction Filter",
  "h2": "Adaptive Trend Band S/R \u2013 Band Fill",
  "h3": ""
},
{
