  "h3": ""
},
{
  "type": "list_item",

},
{
  "type": "list_item",
  "text": "Neutral-Bias: If the slope of the VWAP near 0 (or -0.1 to +0.1) that\u2019s evidence the market is non-trending. Even if it is trending that trend is not supported by the smart money. That could be exhaustion sign. If the market is already near mean (VWAP) and the slope is near 0 and color is Goldenrod that a sign the market is in compression at a neutral point and is going to look for further data to move in some direction or breakout from this compression.",
  "h1": "Atlas VWAP \u2013 Volume-Weighted Average Price",
  "h2": "Smart Money Market-Bias \u2013 Slope m",
  "h3": ""
},
{
  "type": "list_item",

},
{
  "type": "list_item",
  "text": "Market Volumes \u2013 Open & Close: As highlighted earlier, the large institutions have very high volumes to be traded. In order or avoid market chaos they usually slice their trades in chunks, mostly they try to execute majority of their trades within the initial balance period \u2013 first 15-min to half-hour within market open (9:30a \u2013 10:00a \u2013 ET) or during the last half before market close (3:30p \u2013 4:00p \u2013 ET). Therefore, this during this time the VWAP is going to have a trending slope whereas around midday the volumes are lower and VWAP could tend to be flat.",
  "h1": "Atlas VWAP \u2013 Volume-Weighted Average Price",
  "h2": "Smart Money Market-Bias \u2013 Slope m",
  "h3": ""
},
{

  "h3": ""
},
{
  "type": "paragraph",
  "text": "Please ensure to check the numeric value of slope m as listed in the Atlas Regime Dashboard which is a tabulation near top of the chart and there is a cell in the table dedicated for VWAP. Please see VWAP figure above. Do not rely on the visual slope of the line on the chart. As these are Altas Renko charts, sometime the VWAP might seem sloping higher or lower, but the color of the VWAP is still goldenrod. That means the price might be moving very slow in time or the price is moving higher (or lower) with very little volume. That represents a Flat-Market. Upon failure or exhaustion to trend further a mean-reversion of the market back to VWAP becomes probable.",

{
  "type": "paragraph",
  "text": "Usually, VWAP breakout trade entries need to be careful. When a move is happening towards the VWAP and the market bias and momentum stipulates for a VWAP level breakout (break down continuation or break higher continuation) it\u2019s important to recognize that VWAP line is where large institutions have placed high liquidity. So, any approaching rally that results in crossing over the VWAP level would result in immediate exhaustion of the rally and reverting to the VWAP. To trade this, it\u2019s therefore better to wait for the re-bounce as an entry.",
