  "text": "Cumulative Volume Delta (CVD) is an order flow indicator that tracks the running Net Flow difference between aggressive buying (market orders hitting the ask) and aggressive selling (market orders hitting the bid) over time revealing market sentiment and potential price movements. It exposes whether buyers or sellers truly drive price action. The session CVD represents the cumulative Net Delta value on the Future (ES / NQ) starting from 6p \u2013 ET the previous evening. The negative values represent Net selling pressure whereas the positive CVD\u2019s show the Net Buying on the Future. While looked at both markets shows the Net Buy/Sell positions of the traders.",
