## 9. Observability and Audit

Every automated AI workflow should emit or preserve:

- run ID and date;
- AWS region and account;
- workload name;
- model ID and inference profile;
- input source identifiers, not secrets;
- start/end time and duration;
- retry count and error class;
- schema validation result;
- fallback/neutral result count;
- output artifact key and hash;
- CloudFront invalidation ID when applicable.

Recommended CloudWatch metrics:

- `BedrockInvocationCount`
- `BedrockFailureCount`
- `BedrockRetryCount`
- `BedrockLatencyMs`
- `BedrockInvalidOutputCount`
- `NeutralFallbackCount`
- `ReportPublishSuccess`
- `ReportPublishFailure`
- `RouteValidationFailure`
- `DataFreshnessSeconds`

Do not log full credentials, authorization headers, raw user tokens, or unnecessary proprietary document contents.

